From 0fa08c5922b24a638806b96fc872783a94e6579f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:18:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): Fanuc rigid tap option writes M29 S before G84

A new Fanuc post option, rigidTapM29 (off by default), writes
M29 S<rpm> on the block right before each G84 block that opens a cycle
group. G80 ends rigid mode, so each group states it again. A section
with no spindle speed is refused by name, not posted with M29 S0.

Off by default keeps every golden unchanged: a control with parameter
5200 bit 0 set taps rigid on G84 alone.

Refs #2603

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
